<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lithuanian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lithuania is a country on the Baltic coast that was the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>, once one of the largest states in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The Grand Duchy entered a personal union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1386 and was joined with it by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin">Union of Lublin</a> in 1569, forming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. Lithuanian lands remained a distinct component of the Commonwealth until its partitions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuania.jpg" alt="Lithuania" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Jonas Basanavičius, Tadas Daugirdas and Antanas Žmuidzinavičius Vector: SKopp The SVG code is valid. This f... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lithuania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
